INT. OFFICE SUPPLY CLOSET WITH A BIRTHDAY PARTY - DAY

A closet turned party room. Paper streamers. A sheet cake on a filing box. Fluorescent hum. A banner: HAPPY 5TH ANNIVERSARY OF THE REORG.

GLORIA PETROSYAN, 50s, regional manager, lanyard heavy with badges, cuts cake into identical squares. DESMOND "DEZ" ADEYEMI, 30s, tie loosened, scrolls his phone. PRIYA NAIR, 20s, intern, holds a stack of paper plates like a shield.

A TALL MAN in a gray suit leans in the doorway. Clipboard. No smile. Nobody knows him.

GLORIA
Cake?

DEZ
I'm good.

PRIYA
I'll take his. If he's not.

GLORIA
Take two.

Priya takes two. Eats one standing. Dez keeps scrolling.

TALL MAN
Is this the Q3 alignment huddle?

GLORIA
It's cake.

TALL MAN
But is it a huddle?

DEZ
(muttering)
Everything's a huddle.

PRIYA
Is that bad?

DEZ
It's Tuesday.

The Tall Man writes something. Gloria slides a square toward him. He doesn't take it.

GLORIA
You're with Compliance?

TALL MAN
Efficiency.

DEZ
Same floor as Compliance.

TALL MAN
Different elevator.

Priya laughs. Stops. Looks at Gloria. Gloria is not laughing.

GLORIA
Name?

TALL MAN
Hollis. Bertram Hollis.

GLORIA
Mr. Hollis. Cake?

BERTRAM
(softening)
Fine. A small one.

She hands him a plate. He eats. Chews slowly. Dez finally pockets his phone.

DEZ
So what's being made efficient?

BERTRAM
Closets.

PRIYA
This closet?

BERTRAM
Any closet.

Gloria and Dez trade a look. Priya stuffs the second square in her mouth whole.

GLORIA
We use this one.

BERTRAM
For parties.

GLORIA
For morale.

BERTRAM
Morale isn't a line item.

DEZ
Neither is you.

Silence. Priya swallows. Bertram caps his pen, uncaps it.

BERTRAM
I'll note the cake.

GLORIA
Note the frosting. It's lemon.

BERTRAM
Lemon.

PRIYA
Lemon's her mother's recipe.

GLORIA
It's not.

PRIYA
Oh.

The door swings. A cart of toner cartridges rolls in, pushed by nobody visible. Everyone steps back. The cart bumps the cake box. Cake wobbles.

All four grab at the box. Dez catches the front corner. Priya the back. Gloria the cake. Bertram the banner. Everything holds.

They stand like that. Breathing.

DEZ
Nobody say anything.

BERTRAM
I wasn't going to.

GLORIA
Mr. Hollis, you're holding a banner.

BERTRAM
So I am.

He doesn't let go. Neither does anyone else. The fluorescent hum fills the closet.

PRIYA
Is this the huddle?

BERTRAM
(dry)
Yes.

GLORIA
Then I'd say alignment is achieved.

Dez snorts. Priya giggles. Bertram, against his will, almost smiles. The cart's wheel squeaks once, and a tiny voice calls from behind the toner.

MAILROOM KID (O.S.)
Sorry! Sorry. Is that Gloria's closet?

GLORIA
(calling)
It's everyone's closet.

MAILROOM KID (O.S.)
Cool. Also there's cake?

Gloria hands Priya the knife.

GLORIA
Cut another.
